\n\nScreen layout plan:\n\n**01_Home**\n- Status bar (instance, dark glyphs on light bg — default black is fine).\n- Header: greeting? Must include: Balance $3,821 with Icon_Safe, Vulcan Bank payment card (no number), 2 pages current 1, actions row (My card, Transfer, Mobile, search), History section with \"History\", \"TODAY\", 3 rows, tab bar current Main.\n- Layout: \n  - Top: small \"Vulcan Bank\" wordmark + maybe search icon right? The search is listed under Actions with Icon_Search — it's one of the 4 quick actions: My card / Transfer / Mobile / search history.\n  - Balance card: white surface, Icon_Safe, \"Total balance\" label, \"$3,821\" big, pager dots (2 pages, current 1), and a mini Vulcan Bank payment card visual (brand red gradient card with \"Vulcan Bank\" text, no number).\n  - Actually \"Balance: $3,821 (Icon_Safe) · Vulcan Bank payment card (no number shown) · 2 pages, current: 1\" — this is a pager with 2 pages; page 1 shows balance + card. I'll make a horizontal card: balance card containing safe icon, $3,821, and a small red payment card graphic; pager dots below (2 dots, first active).\n  - Quick actions row: 4 items with icon in soft circle + label: My card, Transfer, Mobile, Search (label \"Search\").\n  - History: header row \"History\" + maybe \"See all\"? Not required. \"TODAY\" section label, then 3 rows:\n    1. Airbnb · Payments · −$560 · Icon_Location\n    2. to Anna Nelsen · Transfer · −$380 · Icon_Transfer\n    3. from Anna Nelsen · Transfer · +$470 · Icon_Transfer_In\n  - Tab bar at bottom with home indicator below? Home indicator is part of shell — place at very bottom. Tab bar above it.\n\n**02_About_Investment**\n- No tab bar. Header: back (Icon_Back) left, title \"Investment\"? The copy: \"Investment\" + two paragraphs: \"I will help you create an investment portfolio in less than five minutes!\" and \"Have you wanted to invest in the shares of global giants for a long time? Now it is possible by opening a brokerage account. Let's start!\"\n- Illustration_Investment centered, big.\n- Bottom: brand button \"Start\" with Icon_Arrow_Right (start action uses Icon_Arrow_Right). I'll put arrow icon inside/next to button. Use given Button component instance (374×56, radius 16, \"Continue\" text → override to \"Start\"), plus arrow right icon white inside.\n- Layout: back button top-left (in a circle), illustration center, \"Investment\" big title, paragraphs, button at bottom.\n\n**03_Create_PIN**\n- Header: back + \"Create PIN code\" title.\n- PIN: 4 positions, 3 entered (9·7·7), 4th empty. Show 4 dots — 3 filled, 1 empty. Maybe show digits? Typically dots. But \"3 entered (9 · 7 · 7)\" — I could show digits in circles? Dots are safer visually; but data accuracy — maybe show digits? I'll show circles with numbers 9,7,7 and 4th empty circle. Actually typical PIN shows dots. The must-include says \"PIN: 4 positions · 3 entered (9 · 7 · 7) · 4th empty\". I'll render 4 boxes; first three contain the digits 9,7,7 (visible), 4th is empty outline. That matches data verbatim and shows state clearly.\n- Keypad: 1-9 with letters (2 ABC, 3 DEF, 4 GHI, 5 JKL, 6 MNO, 7 PQRS, 8 TUV, 9 WXYZ), 0 at bottom center, delete (Icon_Backspace) bottom right.\n- \"Ready\" action — brand button at bottom? But keypad occupies bottom. Layout: title, PIN dots, keypad, and \"Ready\" as a text button or button above keypad. I'll place \"Ready\" as a brand text button below PIN dots, right side; or full-width button between PIN and keypad. Space is tight in 896 height: status 44, header ~56, PIN ~80, ready button 56, keypad ~ 4 rows × 72 = 288 + gaps. Total ≈ 44+56+80+16+56+288+home 34 = 574. Fine.\n\n**04_Portfolio**\n- Header: back, \"Investment Portfolio\", right icons: menu, chart (with unread dot), insights.\n- Summary: \"Total earning\" $87,875 +10%; \"Profit\" $28,160 +32%. Two summary cards or one card with two columns.\n- Chart: monthly earnings Mar–Sep, axis 0/50k/100k — bar chart with 7 bars.\n- Cases: \"Cases\" section header; rows for AAPL, TSLA, NFLX, MSFT with logo, price, change. May scroll vertically — frame can be taller? \"04_Portfolio may scroll vertically\" — I can make the frame taller than 896? Canvas is 414×896; scrolling means content taller — I could make the frame 896 tall with content clipped and use scroll in prototype, but simplest: make the frame taller (e.g., 1100) to show all content. Hmm, the brief says canvas 414×896 and \"04_Portfolio may scroll vertically\" meaning it's allowed to have scrollable content; for a static design, making the frame taller is acceptable but the name says canvas fixed. Safer: keep 414×896 and fit everything — 4 stock rows + chart + summary. Let's compute: status 44, header 56, summary ~90, chart ~180, cases header 30, 4 rows × 64 = 256, tab bar 64, home 34 → 754 + paddings ≈ 850. Fits in 896. Good, keep 896.\n- Tab bar current Invest.\n\n**05_Trading**\n- Header: back, \"Trading\", menu, chart, insights (no unread dot mentioned here).\n- Stock: AAPL, Apple Inc., $143.43, +31.62 (28.28%), Logo_Apple.\n- Period selector: Day Week Month Year All, current Day.\n- Chart: candlesticks 10am–3pm, axis $100–$150 step $10.\n- Position: Market Value $97.83, Buying Power $18,943.43.\n- Actions: Buy (Icon_Arrow_Up), Sell (Icon_Arrow_Down) — two buttons, Buy brand red? Typically Buy green / Sell red. Brand is red... I'll make Buy solid brand red? Hmm, red usually = sell. But brand color is persian red. Buy = brand color (primary action), Sell = neutral outline with red? Let me do Buy solid brand (#FA5555), Sell soft/neutral dark outline. That's consistent with \"buy/sell actions are yours\".\n- Tab bar current Invest.\n\n**06_Stock_Transaction**\n- Header: back, \"Stock transaction\", menu.\n- Stock: Apple Inc. AAPL $143.43 +31.62 (28.28%) Logo_Apple.\n- Account: \"ACCOUNT\" label; USD $18,943.43 (selected, checkmark or radio), EUR €16,473.11.\n- Form: \"Quantity\" 1 with hint \"1 lot = 1 stock\"; \"Price\" $143.43 with hints \"1 unit = $143.43\" · \"commission $14.34\". Use Text Field component instances (label + input).\n- Action: \"Buy\" button (Button instance).\n- Tab bar current Invest.\n\n**07_Confirm_Purchase**\n- Dialog over 06_Stock_Transaction: dimmed overlay + centered dialog \"Are you sure?\" with Cancel and Buy buttons. The frame shows 06 behind dimmed. Build by copying 06 content into 07 frame? That's heavy. Alternative: create 07 frame 414×896, place a screenshot-like reconstruction... I need actual nodes. Best approach: after building 06, clone the whole frame, rename to 07_Confirm_Purchase, then add overlay + dialog on top. Cloning preserves instance references. \n\nPrototype links:\n- 01 Invest tab → 02\n- 02 start → 03; back → 01\n- 03 Ready → 04; back → 02\n- 04 AAPL case → 05; back → 01; Main tab → 01\n- 05 Buy → 06; back → 04\n- 06 Buy → 07; back → 05\n- 07 Cancel → 06; Buy → entry only (no link, or link nowhere). \"Buy (entry only — the purchase result is not part of this task)\" means no destination. I'll leave Buy without link (or could add link to nothing). Leave unlinked.\n\nNow execute. Next call: create reusable components. I'll write helper code inline. Because each use_figma call is a fresh JS context, I must re-define helpers each time and reference nodes by ID returned from previous calls.\n\nLet me design component creation code carefully.\n\nComponent 1: TabBar (414 wide, height 64). Tabs: Main, Payments, Cashback, Invest, More. Each tab: icon 24 + label 10px. Current: Main (brand color icon+label, others gray). For current=Invest variant, I'll create instances on 04-06 and override colors of Invest icon/label and reset Main to gray.\n\nSince icons are components themselves, inside TabBar I place instances. To recolor an icon instance: instance children are vector networks; icon components likely have a vector child with fill #1A1A1F. I can set fills on the instance's children? For COMPONENT instances, you can override child fills: find descendants and set fills. Y