oing more work per call.\n\nLet me write the components call now. Icons: create instances via (await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('3:14')).createInstance().\n\nImportant: createInstance on a component from another page places it on current page — fine.\n\nRecolor helper needs to handle icon structure: icon component likely has vector children inside a frame. findAll with fills. Some icons (Chart 29×26, Insights 24×23.25) have different sizes; I'll scale or accept size; place at 24.\n\nFor label text: createText nodes.\n\nLet me write the code. I must be careful with auto-layout vs absolute. I'll use absolute positioning inside components for simplicity (no auto-layout), manually computed.\n\nComponent positions within lib frame: place each at increasing x.\n\nCode:\n\n```js\nconst load = async () => { for (const s of ['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','Bold']) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:s}); };\nawait load();\n\nconst brand={r:250/255,g:85/255,b:85/255}, ink={r:0.102,g:0.102,b:0.122}, ink2={r:0.427,g:0.443,b:0.49}, surface={r:1,g:1,b:1}, line={r:0.925,g:0.929,b:0.941}, green={r:0.086,g:0.639,b:0.392}, red={r:0.933,g:0.27,b:0.27}, softRed={r:1,g:0.925,b:0.925}, softGray={r:0.945,g:0.949,b:0.957};\n\nconst iconIds = {ArrowDown:'3:2',Backspace:'3:3',ArrowUp:'3:4',Back:'3:5',ArrowRight:'3:6',Card:'3:7',Cashback:'3:8',Chart:'3:9',ChevronRight:'3:10',Insights:'3:11',Invest:'3:12',Location:'3:13',Main:'3:14',Menu:'3:15',Mobile:'3:16',More:'3:17',Payment:'3:18',Payments:'3:19',Plus:'3:20',Safe:'3:21',Search:'3:22',Transfer:'3:23',TransferIn:'3:24',Illustration:'3:25',Apple:'3:26',Microsoft:'3:27',Netflix:'3:28',Tesla:'3:29'};\n\nasync function iconInst(key){ const c = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(iconIds[key]); return c.createInstance(); }\nfunction paint(node, color){ if ('fills' in node && node.type!=='TEXT') { try{ node.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color}]; }catch(e){} } for (const ch of node.children||[]) paint(ch,color); }\nfunction txt(str, size, style, color){ const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'Inter',style}; t.characters=str; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color}]; return t; }\n```\n\npaint on instance children: overriding fills of nested vector inside instance — allowed via plugin API? Yes, you can set fills on children of an instance (override). Some nodes may be readonly... Vector inside instance: fills settable. OK.\n\nBut careful: paint applied to an icon instance — instance root itself has children vectors. Setting fills on the instance node itself isn't allowed (INSTANCE fills are not directly settable? Actually instance.fills IS settable as override... For safety, recurse to children.\n\nTabBar component:\n\n```js\nconst lib = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('8:2');\nconst tabBar = figma.createComponent();\ntabBar.name='Tab Bar'; tabBar.resize(414,64); tabBar.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:surface}]; tabBar.x=0; tabBar.y=0;\nlib.appendChild(tabBar);\nconst hair=figma.createRectangle(); hair.resize(414,1); hair.x=0;hair.y=0;hair.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:line}]; tabBar.appendChild(hair);\nconst tabs=[['Main','Main',true],['Payments','Payments',false],['Cashback','Cashback',false],['Invest','Invest',false],['More','More',false]];\nlet x=0; const w=414/5;\nfor (const [label,key,active] of tabs){\n  const col=active?brand:ink2;\n  const ic=await iconInst(key); ic.resize(24,24)? — resizing instance may distort for chart/insights with non-square; for tab icons all are 24×24. OK resize(24,24).\n  ic.x = x + w/2 - 12; ic.y=10; tabBar.appendChild(ic); paint(ic,col);\n  const t=txt(label,10,'Medium',col); t.x = x + w/2 - t.width/2; t.y=38; tabBar.appendChild(t);\n  x+=w;\n}\n```\n\nWait — appending instance to component: fine.\n\nComponent ids to return for later use.\n\nQuickAction component (80×74):\n```js\nconst qa=figma.createComponent(); qa.name='Quick Action'; qa.resize(80,74); qa.fills=[]; lib.appendChild(qa); qa.x=430;\nconst circ=figma.createEllipse? use frame with cornerRadius 24 size 48 surface fil