{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":35196,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"080b6ae868e90a7a16d44e13de4bf4d6","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Disaster — `figma.currentPage` is now \"00 · Start Here\"?? It shows \"Start Here · Brief\" as a child of the current page. So currentPage is the Start Here page, not Workspace! That means my earlier `setCurrentPageAsync` worked, but a later call (the rate-limit error ones) may have... no wait. Let me think.\n\nActually — the concerning part: earlier calls appended `lib` (Components frame 8:2) and components 9:2 etc to \"figma.currentPage\". And the screen build appended 01_Home to figma.currentPage. If currentPage at those times was correctly Workspace (5:2), fine. But now currentPage appears to be the Start Here page.\n\nHmm, but getNodeByIdAsync('8:2') worked earlier... Did all my components get appended to the WRONG page (00 Start Here)? The error \"Removing this node is not allowed\" happened when calling `oldIc.remove()` on an instance child — that's because you can't remove children of an instance. OK that explains the remove error.\n\nBut the bigger issue: is currentPage really Start Here now? The listing shows current page children = [Start Here · Brief (4:2)]. Node 4:2 is the brief frame, which lives on page 0:1. So figma.currentPage === page 0:1 (Start Here). \n\nPossibly the plugin context's currentPage resets between tool calls to whatever page the user has open in the editor (page 0:1, the first page). My setCurrentPageAsync succeeded (\"ok true, page 03 Workspace\") — but then subsequent calls may have currentPage reverted?? Actually each use_figma call runs a fresh plugin instance; figma.currentPage at start = the page the user is viewing in Figma = 0:1.\n\nSo: the components lib (8:2) and 01_Home frame... wait, 01_Home failed midway (remove error) so the whole execution aborted — but nodes created before the error persist. Where did they get appended? In that execution, currentPage was whatever it was — likely 0:1! So my 01_Home partial frame might be appended to page 0:1 (Start Here)!! That would violate \"preserve reference pages\". I need to check and clean up.\n\nAlso lib (8:2) and components (9:*) were appended in executions where currentPage might also have been 0:1... The first call created lib and appended to figma.currentPage — at that time I hadn't set page yet; the previous setCurrentPageAsync call happened in a different plugin run, so currentPage was 0:1 there too?? But wait — the setCurrentPageAsync returned \"03 · Workspace\" and that was its own run. Page switching may persist in the editor between runs (setCurrentPageAsync changes the editor's active page). Hmm, it did persist for... unclear.\n\nLet me check: find nodes 8:2, 9:2, and any 01_Home frame; check their parents. Then move everything to Workspace and clean Start Here page. Use figma.getNodeByIdAsync and check .parent.id.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a558fc7-699a-4150-ad66-1b2df7225d3f","uuid":"4936f1cf-d0e1-4723-b046-437e3850c76b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:42:01.165Z","thinking_duration_ms":13231}
